Fort de plus de 13 ans d’expérience en R&D, Pellenc Energy associe chimie des cellules et électronique embarquée pour développer, grâce à ses technologies brevetées, des batteries intelligentes plus performantes, plus sûres et plus durables. Il ambitionne de commercialiser ses solutions pour les véhicules électriques, le stockage résidentiel, le médical, les drones et l’outillage électroportatif professionnel.
 Recherche son Responsable Electronique hardware & software H/F. 
 Sous la responsabilité hiérarchique du Directeur Général, vous serez le garant du développement du pôle R&D Electronique en pilotant une équipe pluridisciplinaire (Ingénieurs hardware et software, Chargés d'Affaire en électronique) et superviserez la conduite des projets du pôle Electronique.
 Vos principales missions seront : 
 ·      Développer et consolider les structures hardware des différentes versions du projet PREDYCE en lien avec les industries de la mobilité et de la sécurité ;
 ·      Garantir le suivi et l’avancement du Projet, (communication, suivi et respect des délais, suivi et respect du budget, reporting) en informer la Direction de son avancée et participer à son orientation stratégique ;
 ·      Rédiger et/ou participer à la rédaction des contrats de collaboration avec les partenaires externes ;
 ·      Participer à la Protection Intellectuelle : rédiger et/ou participer à la rédaction des enveloppes Soleau, brevets ;
 ·      Participer à la veille technique (brevets, publication, etc..) ;
 ·      Rédiger le rapport annuel du Crédit Impôt Recherche (CIR) et contrôler le pointage des heures de son équipe ;
 ·      Participer au recrutement des collaborateurs de son équipe projet (rédaction fiche de poste, entretiens de recrutement, décisions) ;
 ·      Réaliser les entretiens annuels de son équipe projet et les remonter à son N+1 ;
 ·      Garantir l'archivage des travaux dans l'arborescence réseau ;
 ·      Respecter les règles QHSE.
 De formation Ingénieur en Électronique et Informatique embarquée ou équivalent, vous cumulez 10 années d’expérience réussies minimum, et avez idéalement une première expérience en 
 Electronique automobile ou électronique de défense.  Vous avez une bonne maîtrise de la programmation informatique hardware C/C++, logiciels de conception électronique : CAO/DAO, simulation LTSpice/Spice. 
 Leader, agile et pro actif, vous avez de vraies capacités d’encadrement et de solides qualités humaines et relationnelles. Diplomate et ouvert d’esprit, vous êtes curieux et êtes véritablement passionné par l’électronique. Vous souhaitez rejoindre une société en développement et contribuer activement à un projet collectif ambitieux et innovant ! 
 Anglais lu, parlé et écrit couramment obligatoire.

Job Description
 In Digital Solutions, we drive innovation for connected mobility and deliver cutting-edge digital products to our global fleet customers. As a Data Engineer, you will play a key role in building and optimizing data platforms and pipelines that power AI-driven solutions for our global fleet customers.
 You will design, develop, and maintain scalable data infrastructures, ensuring seamless integration of IoT and telematics data from connected tires and vehicles. Working closely with Data Scientists, MLOps Engineers, and cross-functional teams, you will enable advanced analytics and machine learning capabilities that enhance safety, reduce costs, and extend tire lifecycle.
 Key responsibilities :
 Design, build, and maintain scalable data pipelines for real-time and batch processing of IoT and telematics data;
 Develop and manage cloud-based data platforms, optimizing workflows for performance, scalability, and cost efficiency;
 Implement data quality, validation, and governance processes, ensuring compliance with security and privacy regulations (e.g., GDPR);
 Collaborate with Data Scientists and MLOps Engineers to deliver reliable datasets and support end-to-end AI/ML services;
 Mentor junior engineers, review work, and organize knowledge-sharing sessions to foster best practices.
 Additional Information
 Our offer:
 Integration in a challenging and international work environment;
 Flexible working model;
 Collaborative working style;
 Continuous opportunities for the promotion of talent and training;
 Opportunity to make a difference.
 We are committed to fostering a workplace where everyone feels safe, respected, and valued. All kind of applications are welcome.
 Ready to drive with Continental? Take the first step and fill in the online application.
 Qualifications
 Academic degree in Computer Science, IT, Engineering, Mathematics, or related field;
 >2 years of experience as a Data Engineer;
 Strong programming skills in Python and SQL;
 Expertise in data pipelining (AirFlow);
 Hands-on experience with big data and distributed processing frameworks (e.g., Spark, Databricks, Hadoop, Kafka, DBT);
 Solid understanding of data modeling and databases (relational, NoSQL, time-series);
 Familiarity with data versioning and lineage tracking;
 Experience with Agile project management methods (Scrum, Kanban);
 Experience working in an international team (desirable);
 Reliable team player with structured self-organized workstyle;
 Proficient English language skills (spoken / written).
 Company Description
 Continental is a leading tire manufacturer and industry specialist that develops and produces sustainable, safe and convenient solutions for automotive manufacturers as well as industrial and end customers worldwide. Founded in 1871, the company generated sales of €19.7 billion in 2025 and currently employs around 78,000 people in 54 countries and markets.

Job Description
 The IT Competence Center Supply Chain Management provides solutions for the global Supply Chain Planning at Continental Tires. We drive Artificial Intelligence based projects in this area to efficiently manage the growing complexity in a volatile business environment.
 We are currently seeking a dedicated AWS Cloud Engineer for the enhancement, maintenance and roll-out of our AI forecasting solution.
 Did we spark your interest? We are looking forward to getting to know you.
 Main Responsibilities: 
 Building and providing mechanisms to implement solution environments using Infrastructure-as-Code approaches (IaC) with AWS cloud resources;
 Executing and automating regular maintenance activities for the department’s cloud infrastructure;
 Monitoring and analyzing workloads (on virtual machines and containers) with focus on reliability, performance and maintainability;
 Implementing central cybersecurity policies for department solutions;
 Evaluating and implementing cloud-based technologies and architectures to support AI and machine learning initiatives;
 Guiding our internal team with respect to infrastructure-related topics;
 Coordinating technical support activities and engaging with AWS Support to resolve infrastructure-related incidents and service issues.
 Additional Information
 Our offer:
 Integration in a challenging and international work environment;
 Flexible working model;
 Collaborative working style;
 Continuous opportunities for the promotion of talent and training;
 Opportunity to make a difference.
 We are committed to fostering a workplace where everyone feels safe, respected, and valued. All kind of applications are welcome.
 Ready to drive with Continental? Take the first step and fill in the online application.
 Qualifications
 Academic degree in Computer Science, Business Informatics, Software Engineering or comparable study;
 First working experience in IT infrastructure, including networking, virtualization, storage solutions and AWS cloud platform;
 General working knowledge in Linux environments (preferably RHEL and clones, like Oracle Linux);
 Base knowledge in software development and scripting (mainly in Bash scripting and Typescript/JavaScript programming);
 First experience with Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) implementations (ideally with AWS CDK or AWS CloudFormation);
 Experience in Git-based version control workflows;
 Experience with Oracle databases is a plus;
 First experience with container-based environments like Docker / Kubernetes is a plus;
 Process-oriented mindset and analytical thinking skills;
 Clear and effective communication skills;
 Goal- and team-oriented working style;
 Proficiency in English language skills (written / verbal).
